@xiongzubiao it is not required to use the NVIDIA Container Runtime when using native CDI support in a container engine such as cri-o or containerd. As you have already demonstrated when not using the GPU Operator.

The reason for using the `nvidia.cdi.k8s.io` prefix over the `cdi.k8s.io` that is enabled by default by CRI-O is that we are required to support a wide range of container engine versions. To do so we use the NVIDIA Container Runtime (in CDI mode) to make the required modifications to the incoming OCI runtime specification. The custom prefix ensures that these modifications are not ALSO made by Containerd or Crio.

We are looking at the implications of making use of native CDI support in engines such as containerd or CRI-O instead.

